            children: [
              {
                id: "text-2",
                type: "text",
                body: "In this segment, we will explore the derivation of the Maxwell equations' transformation for"
              },
              {
                id: "text-3",
                type: "text",
                body: "a general velocity boost in any given direction."
              },
              {
                id: "text-4",
                type: "text",
                body: "Traditionally, the derivation of relativistic Maxwell equations is tackled through"
              },
              {
                id: "text-5",
                type: "text",
                body: "differential geometry. Einstein's seminal work utilized standard multivariate calculus, albeit"
              },
              {
                id: "text-6",
                type: "text",
                body: "limited to boosts aligned with coordinate axes. Extending this to boosts in arbitrary"
              },
              {
                id: "text-7",
                type: "text",
                body: "directions significantly complicates the calculus involved, a topic seldom addressed in"
              },
              {
                id: "text-8",
                type: "text",
                body: "existing literature or online resources."
              },
              {
                id: "text-9",
                type: "text",
                body: "Our journey through the relativistic Maxwell equations will be rooted in multivariate"
              },
              {
                id: "text-10",
                type: "text",
                body: "calculus. The foundational definitions and indispensable formulas will be laid out in the"
              },
              {
                id: "text-11",
                type: "text",
                body: "opening section, setting the stage for the intricate derivations that follow."
              },
              {
                id: "text-12",
                type: "text",
                body: "The subsequent section delves into the transformation of key differential operators---divergence"
              },
              {
                id: "text-13",
                type: "text",
                body: "and curl---under the Lorentz transformation, a pivotal step in understanding the equations'"
              },
              {
                id: "text-14",
                type: "text",
                body: "behaviour under relativistic conditions."
              },
              {
                id: "text-15",
                type: "text",
                body: "Culminating in the final section, we will tackle the derivation of the relativistic Maxwell"
              },
              {
                id: "text-16",
                type: "text",
                body: "equations within a realm devoid of charges and currents, showcasing the equations' purest"
              },
              {
                id: "text-17",
                type: "text",
                body: "form in a charge-free vacuum."
              }
            ]
